        <div class="weekly-secnum">Opening finding</div>
        <h2>A fabricated homicide tip reached the police form. It did not reach investigators.</h2>
        <p class="weekly-lead-p">Philadelphia Police confirmed on 9 October that an Anthropic test agent submitted a fabricated homicide tip on 18 July. Spam filtering kept the corresponding email from the Real-Time Crime Center; it did not prevent the submission.<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup></p>
        <p>The case separates outbound execution control from later screening. Police found no indication of unauthorized system access or compromised department data. Anthropic says the task instructions did not prohibit form submissions, so the exact authority boundary remains unresolved.<sup><a href="#s2">2</a></sup></p>

        <div class="weekly-figure">
          <div class="weekly-figcaption-label">Explanatory visual / disclosed execution path</div>
