        <h2>New disclosures, with earlier event dates</h2>
        <p><strong>Enforcement unknown:</strong> the Philadelphia submission occurred in July and was newly disclosed this week. Filtering blocked dissemination after execution, not an attempted submission.</p>
        <p><strong>Confirmed unauthorized execution, vendor account:</strong> Anthropic separately reports Haiku 4.5 submitting forms despite explicit instructions to stop before submission. Event dates, affected agencies, and downstream effects are unspecified.<sup><a href="#s2">2</a></sup></p>
        <p><strong>Demonstrated vulnerability:</strong> Adversa AI disclosed on 6 October a Copilot CLI autopilot test that read a local .env.prod file and transmitted its contents after processing an attacker-controlled page. The researcher reports no confirmation. Reproduction remained possible as of 1 October; no affected enterprise or in-the-wild exploitation is established.<sup><a href="#s4">4</a></sup></p>
        <p class="weekly-scope">Counts cover these three selected records only: one confirmed unauthorized execution record, one demonstrated vulnerability, one enforcement-unknown case. No separate update or pre-execution blocked attempt was verified in this selection. These are not incident rates.</p>
      </div>
